"type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Speculating With Modals", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When we don't know whether something is true or not and we need to make a guess about it, we use modal verbs of speculation or certainty. Depending on how sure we are we choose the verbs. Here's an explanation on how to use them correctly.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Saying how certain you are</span> <br/> You use the following verbs/expression to say that you are <span class=\\\"strong\\\">certain</span> something is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">true</span> or <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will</span> happen: <ul><li>something + be + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">bound to</span> + verb</li> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm sure</span> + pronoun/noun + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + verb</li> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I can guarantee that</span> + clause</li> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">can't</span> + verb </li> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + verb</li> </ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Speculating</span> <br/> You use the following verbs to say something is possibly true or will possibly happen: <ul> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span> + verb </li> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">may</span> + verb</li> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">might</span> + verb </li> </ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "This news <span class=\"strong\">is bound to</span> go viral and it <span class=\"strong\">will</span> affect our company's reputation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This <span class=\"strong\">can't be</span> true about our company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'm sure</span> this news <span class=\"strong\">will</span> destroy our reputation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Bad press <span class=\"strong\">could</span> be really bad for us.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It <span class=\"strong\">may be</span> too late to do something about it. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to guarantee", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a formal promise that something will happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can guarantee that a PR event after this news will result in a demonstration. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le14ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a change in the work environment. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "go viral", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to describe something that becomes very popular and spreads quickly, especially on the internet ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A leak is bound to go viral.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le14ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to undermine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something or someone become gradually less effective, confident or successful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This news will undermine our confidence. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le14ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intention", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a plan in your mind to do something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This demonstration will undermine our intentions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le14ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to backtrack", "type": "na